<Project>

    <!--
        Solution-wide build defaults.

        XML documentation is generated for every project so that:
          - the API reference (Scalar/OpenAPI) can surface controller and DTO summaries, and
          - the compiler flags documentation that references parameters which no longer exist (CS1572).

        Noise from the convention-driven docs is suppressed:
          - CS1591: missing XML comment for a publicly visible member (we don't document everything).
          - CS1573: a parameter has no matching param tag (params are documented only when not self-evident).
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591;CS1573</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!--
        Analyzer and nullable ratchet.

        Nullable is on for every project. A project that is not annotated yet sets
        <Nullable>disable</Nullable> in its csproj and is listed in build/nullable-allowlist.txt.
        scripts/check-nullable-allowlist.sh fails when the two disagree, so the list can only shrink.
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <AnalysisLevel>latest-recommended</AnalysisLevel>
        <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <!--
        The DroneDB (libddb) build Registry is built and tested against.

        This is the only place it is written. scripts/ddb-release.sh reads it for everything that
        installs libddb, downloads exactly this build and checks it with sha256sum -c:
          - CI installs the .deb (scripts/ddb-release.sh fetch-deb);
          - the Dockerfile installs the same .deb (fetch-deb, token as a build secret for a CI build);
          - Registry.Web.csproj embeds the Windows zip in Windows builds (release: downloaded by
            MSBuild; ci: fetch-windows-zip) and fails the build when its SHA256 differs.
        scripts/ddb-release.sh check (CI) fails when the pin is malformed or written elsewhere, or
        when anything downloads releases/latest. Startup checks the ABI of the loaded library
        (DdbAbi: libddb 2.x, ABI major 2, minor >= 0), not this version number.

        DdbSource:
          release  a published release: DdbVersion, and the SHA256 of ddb_<DdbVersion>_amd64.deb and
                   ddb-<DdbVersion>-Windows.zip (the "digest" of each asset, or SHA256SUMS, in
                   gh api repos/DroneDB/DroneDB/releases/tags/v<version>). Remove the Ci and
                   ArtifactId properties.
          ci       an unreleased DroneDB CI build (c-cpp.yml): the DroneDB commit, its run, the ids
                   of its "Linux-Binaries" and "Windows Binaries" artifacts
                   (gh api repos/DroneDB/DroneDB/actions/runs/<run>/artifacts), DdbVersion as that
                   build names its files, and the SHA256 of the .deb and of the zip inside them.
                   Downloading an artifact needs DRONEDB_ARTIFACT_TOKEN (see scripts/ddb-release.sh);
                   artifacts expire 90 days after their run.

                   DdbDebFileVersion (optional, ci only): the version in the .deb file name when it is
                   not DdbVersion. DroneDB names the .deb of an untagged build <package.json
                   version>~git<commit> (scripts/build-debian-package.sh; the commit is the pull
                   request merge commit for a PR run), e.g. ddb_2.0.0~git1813815_amd64.deb next to
                   ddb-2.0.0-Windows.zip. Remove the property with the move to the release.

        Pinned now (2026-10-28): DroneDB has ONE version, 2.0.0 (package.json); the libddb ABI follows
        it (ABI 2.0, semver: a removed export is a new major, an added one a new minor) and so does
        the handshake (libddb 2.x). It is not tagged until Registry is proven on it, so Registry pins
        the CI build of DroneDB fixes-and-optimizations commit a9f5e43, run 40706550975 (a pull
        request run of DroneDB#472, built from the merge with master; the .deb is named after that
        merge commit, 2.0.0~git77636835), every job green (Linux and Windows builds and tests,
        ASan + UBSan, the Docker image). Each artifact of a build object and a resolved build file
        carry a version (a digest of the opened file's write time and size) that changes whenever
        the file is rewritten under the same hash, which versioned build URLs are cached by;
        build-lod is Spark v2.4.0 and reads every SPZ version, so a v4 upload is no longer
        transcoded first. A build that only waits for companion files the dataset
        lacks (its pending marker lists missing files) is not retried on a timer: DDBIsBuildPending
        counts only work a retry can progress, DDBGetPendingBuildInfo and the build object of
        DDBGetBuildArtifacts / DDBListEntriesEx report awaitingFiles, and adding, moving, delta-applying
        or copying in a file of a missing name releases the build; the build-lod silence limit grows
        with the splats of the source. It exports the two Gaussian splat exports Registry calls
        and the startup handshake requires: DDBExportSplatSpz (the .spz of a splat for other tools,
        made on demand in the build folder as gsplat/export.spz, role gsplat.export) and
        DDBExportSplatTrainingData (the COLMAP sparse model, the images and the georeference of an
        ODM project). DDBResolveBuildFile returns {"path", "mediaType"}, the media type of the
        build manifest with the path. Splat builds no longer write into the dataset folder or the
        published folder, build SPZ 4 and .sog uploads, take a .rad upload as it is (published as
        a copy, not a hard link), check the sizes a .rad declares, and survive a bounds.json that
        cannot be written; bounds.json says which way is up, confident only when the splats leave
        no second answer, and a splat (or a model) georeferenced by an ODM coords.txt or a
        georef.json gets up [0, 0, 1] and its WGS84 footprint (wgs84Footprint). Splat thumbnails
        show the subject upright. 3D models are built with the bm3d program from vendor/bm3d at
        release v1.1.1: the output is bm3d/model.bm3d (role model.bm3d), and the Nexus build
        nxs/model.nxz is the legacy role model.nexus with fallbackFor model.bm3d, served while the
        bm3d model is missing and removed once bm3d/ is published. STL files are Models. On Windows
        the programs of the build (ddbcmd.exe, bm3d.exe, metadata-util.exe, untwine.exe) declare
        themselves long path aware, and libddb reads the folder of the executable and of libddb
        whatever the length of its path, so the embedded libddb and its helper programs work in
        datasets under long paths where Windows allows them (LongPathsEnabled). DDBBuildEx (a build
        with a cap on its threads, {"threads": N}, which the background rebuild of models of an
        older layout calls) stays, with GPX and JPEG 2000 files and the formula mask fix of the
        earlier pins. Next: the v2.0.0 release (DdbSource release) once it is tagged.
    -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <DdbSource>ci</DdbSource>
        <DdbVersion>2.0.0</DdbVersion>
        <DdbDebFileVersion>2.0.0~git77636835</DdbDebFileVersion>
        <DdbCiCommit>a9f5e437ca3ad809442ce0d0bdccedec82a4b2a5</DdbCiCommit>
        <DdbCiRunId>40706550975</DdbCiRunId>
        <DdbDebArtifactId>12826677568</DdbDebArtifactId>
        <DdbWindowsArtifactId>12827705682</DdbWindowsArtifactId>
        <DdbDebSha256>22b33e0d5816ecf65d266f5f3a9475dd2925d6b9c5f85ed40252918b0e0f9bb1</DdbDebSha256>
        <DdbWindowsZipSha256>3b24f7ab61e77acb3fb69977d3e349350020d976378c6e1fd23468574e50fb09</DdbWindowsZipSha256>
    </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
